<!-- Real-world purchase order (cXML 1.2, Ariba PUNCHOUT dialect, captured 2026-07-13), de-identified
     for the repo: every trading-party name, network identity, postal address, internal system id,
     requisition number and customer id is a placeholder. Item codes, quantities, currency and money
     are VERBATIM — they are the test signal, and nothing that carries them identifies anybody.

     Why this fixture exists: the order came through a PUNCHOUT session, so the buyer's
     <SupplierPartID> ("29954596") is the buying network's own internal id and resolves against
     nothing in the supplier's catalog. The only usable key is
     <ManufacturerPartID>LTQ2500-BK-BTK1</ManufacturerPartID> + <ManufacturerName>Litware</ManufacturerName>.
     Blindly echoing the manufacturer part number back as the supplier item code is WRONG here —
     it has to be looked up in the catalog and translated into the supplier's own code.
     Pair it with real-cxml-1.1-mpn-equals-supplier-part.xml, the easy case where the two match. -->
